  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is associated with NCI-H522 through a series of molecular interactions involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which acts as a target of multiple kinases. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C may modulate the activity of Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn influences the behavior of NCI-H522. This pathway involves the regulation of serine/threonine-protein kinases, such as ICK and Casein kinase I isoform alpha, which are known to play roles in cellular signaling and may contribute to the biological effects observed in NCI-H522 cells. The scores from the different paths indicate a consistent relationship, with slight variations in confidence levels, likely due to differences in the specific targets and their roles in the cellular context. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Oblonganoside C could exert its effects on NCI-H522, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction."
